ndles all cases correctly. I'll also correct the name to `remove_Occ` as expected.\n\nThus error_location: \"def remove_first_last_occurrence(s, char):\" (wrong function name). error_reason: \"The test code expects the function to be named 'remove_Occ', but the student defined it as 'remove_first_last_occurrence', causing NameError.\"\n\nThen corrected_solution: \n```python\ndef remove_Occ(s, char):\n    first = s.find(char)\n    last = s.rfind(char)\n    if first != -1:\n        if first == last:\n            # Only one occurrence\n            return s[:first] + s[first+1:]\n        else:\n            return s[:first] + s[first+1:last] + s[last+1:]\n    return s\n```\n\nOr simpler: if first == -1: return s; elif first == last: return s[:first]+s[first+1:]; else: return s[:first]+s[first+1:last]+s[last+1:].\n\nI'll output JSON.\n</thinking>\n\n### Phát hiện lỗi\ndef remove_first_last_occurrence(s, char):\n\n### Nguyên nhân\nThe test harness expects the function to be named 'remove_Occ' as shown in the verifier traceback, but the student defined it as 'remove_first_last_occurrence', resulting in a NameError when the test calls remove_Occ.\n\n### Sửa lại\ndef remove_Occ(s, char):\n    first = s.find(char)\n    last = s.rfind(char)\n    if first == -1:\n        return s\n    if first == last:\n        return s[:first] + s[first+1:]\n    return s[:first] + s[first+1:last] + s[last+1:]"}]}
