e corrected solution: import Counter, define function find_Product(arr, n), and same logic. Possibly the test expects the product of only elements that appear exactly once. So corrected_solution should be the code.\n\nWe'll output:\n{\n  \"error_location\": \"def product_of_non_repeated_elements(arr):\",\n  \"error_reason\": \"The student defined the function with the name 'product_of_non_repeated_elements', but the test code expects the function to be named 'find_Product'. This causes a NameError when the verifier tries to call the function.\",\n  \"corrected_solution\": \"from collections import Counter\\n\\ndef find_Product(arr, n):\\n    element_count = Counter(arr)\\n    product = 1\\n    for elem in arr:\\n        if element_count[elem] == 1:\\n            product *= elem\\n    return product\"\n}\n\nWe'll ensure JSON format, no trailing commas.\n</thinking>\n\n### Phát hiện lỗi\ndef product_of_non_repeated_elements(arr):\n\n### Nguyên nhân\nThe student defined the function with the name 'product_of_non_repeated_elements', but the test code calls the function 'find_Product'. This mismatch causes a NameError at runtime.\n\n### Sửa lại\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef find_Product(arr, n):\n    element_count = Counter(arr)\n    product = 1\n    for elem in arr:\n        if element_count[elem] == 1:\n            product *= elem\n    return product"}]}
